   "BIP-021 targets six real bugs across bitecho, but Stage 0 contains production-breaking flaws across five subsystems (plus omissions audited against 74d760f/b072e6a) that will cause cryptographic nonce reuse, permanent session deadlocks, fail-closed HTTP 403s, and stalled/racy auto-updaters if merged as written.\n\n1. §2.4 tx-seq Rollback Recovery, AEAD Nonce Reuse & Node.js fsyncSync Stalls (crypto/sealed.cljc, light_node/core.cljc, node_main.cljs, shell/light_node.clj):\n- Immediate AEAD nonce reuse before session-ack: sealed/seal-message (crypto/sealed.cljc:917) uses a deterministic nonce (seq->nonce seq-num) keyed by (:tx-key session). After a VM snapshot rollback (e.g. tx-seq 20 -> 18), ANY outbound send at seq 19..20 before the peer's session-ack arrives ALREADY reuses (tx-key, nonce(19/20)) under AES-256-GCM (leaking GHASH key H) or ChaCha20-Poly1305. Fast-forwarding tx-seq only on late session-ack while leaving the compromised :tx-key open with merely :reoffer-recommended? true fails to neutralize nonce reuse.\n- Silent deadlock at rollback lag >= 64: check-and-advance-replay-window (crypto/sealed.cljc:1058-1065, default window-size 64) returns :stale-seq (NOT :replayed-seq) once (- highest seq-val) >= 64. handle-wire-sealed-msg (light_node/core.cljc:6847-6861) only checks (= :replayed-seq (:error chk)) and falls through :else at L6860-6861 with zero session-ack, zero fast-forward signal, and zero diagnostics.\n- Outbox data loss & ACK-signature downgrade hazard: in handle-wire-session-ack (light_node/core.cljc:6895), (acked? s) purges outbox entries where (<= s ack-seq). If a locally re-sent post-rollback msg 19' sits in outbox and peer ACKs pre-rollback seq 20, purging before rollback eviction silently deletes un-delivered 19' (since peer deduped it). Additionally, BIP-021's backwards-compatible signature fallback for :peer-high-seq MUST reject old canonical verification whenever :peer-high-seq is present in the payload; otherwise an attacker can graft an arbitrary :peer-high-seq onto a captured legacy ACK signature to force tx-seq jumps and outbox eviction.\n- Blocking .fsyncSync on Node.js event loop: forcing synchronous .fsyncSync (node_main.cljs:1150-1170 write-bytes-atomic!) before flushing outbound envelopes stalls the single-threaded event loop 10-100+ ms per send (violating BIP-014 P-ASYNC-2, starving WebRTC keepalives and /ctl), races against save-light-state-async! (L1246, allowing older async renames to overwrite newer sync tx-seq state), and cannot protect against VM hypervisor snapshot rollbacks that revert disk too.\n\n2. §2.6.2 Mesh-First Auto-Updater Protocol Vacuum, Size Ceilings & Async Stage Race (light_node/core.cljc, deploy/core.cljc, node_main.cljs, full_node_main.cljs, shell/updater.clj, browser_main.cljs):\n- Non-existent RPC & incompatible transport ceilings: exec-artifact-get (light_node/core.cljc:5507-5622) is local-only (:net-envelopes []); validators and mesh nodes implement no light-node RPC handler for remote artifact-get (shell/infra.clj:1545 :peer-fetch-blob is validator-to-validator only). Even if wired, unchunked blobs collide with WebRTC SDP a=max-message-size:262144 (256 KiB SCTP limit), HTTP relay :max-payload-bytes 65536 (64 KiB, core/protocol/relay.cljc:123), and validator /artifact/v1/blob max-chunk-bytes 4 MiB (chunk_constants.cljc + shell/http.clj:2070-2081, compounded by 2x bytes_hex JSON and 4x hex+data_hex /ctl JSON at node_main.cljs:3450 / light_node/core.cljc:5534). Current bitecho-light-node.cjs (~1.7 MiB, scaling toward 3-6 MiB) and JVM uberjars (bitecho.jar, 20-60+ MiB) cannot transfer unchunked over mesh DataChannels/relays and fail 413 payload-too-large over single-blob HTTP once > 4 MiB.\n- Async staging race & wedged :phase :fetching: deploy/core.cljc:1712-1718 returns [:stage-light-bundle ... :atomic-swap-and-restart-light-node ...] in the same :blob-fetched effect list, while node_main.cljs:3654 starts async (.writeFile node-fsp ...) without awaiting completion before :atomic-swap-and-restart-light-node (L3666) spawns node <tmp> --help. Further, :fetch-bundle-blob failures (node_main.cljs:3638-3643, shell/updater.clj:119) never dispatch an error event back into reduce-light-update-tick, leaving updater-atom stuck in :phase :fetching; and full_node_main.cljs:3114-3146 + browser_main.cljs:2475-2545 (single pointerUrl SPOF) are omitted from §2.6.2.\n\n3. §2.5.3 Encrypted Rolodex 403 Fail-Closed & Crypto Bugs (core/infra.cljc, core/subnet.cljc, core/data.cljc, full_node_main.cljs, browser_main.cljs, chat.js):\n- Guaranteed HTTP 403 on live ns1..ns3: full_node_main.cljs POST /artifact/v1/pointer routes solely to the embedded 'bitecho.org/infra' subnet-runtime, and core/data.cljc:742 rejects foreign :pointer/subnet values with :pointer-subnet-mismatch. Meanwhile default-infra-policy (core/infra.cljc:215-243) defines no rolodex/<pubkey>/* ACL entry and enforces :gate/mode :permissioned :allowlist (core/subnet.cljc:356-360), rejecting end-user pubkeys with :not-in-allowlist. Note core/subnet.cljc:98-102 also prohibits :streamlet-bft on :permissionless subnets.\n- Nonce reuse, metadata leakage & hardware keys: deriving AEAD nonces deterministically from local :seq breaks AEAD security whenever IndexedDB is cleared or a second device writes before rolodex-restore; rolodex-put must use random 96-bit CSPRNG :nonce-hex, pre-query remote min_remote_seq, bind AAD (pubkey, seq, schema), and pad ciphertexts (e.g. 4 KiB buckets). Must also handle non-extractable WebAuthn/WebCrypto keys where raw Ed25519 private bytes cannot be exported, and coordinate async restore timing with handleRecoverYubiKey (chat.js:1889-1932) and localStorage hive_subscribed_subnets.\n\n4. §2.6.1 :443 Passthrough Half-Close Drain vs. Overnight arrayBuffers Drift (core/infra.cljc, full_node_main.cljs):\n- full_node_main.cljs:3889-3900 creates front-srv with default allowHalfOpen: false, splice-sockets! (.pipe), and peeking chunks array. Specifying :end-socket + 5000 ms drain without explicitly unpiping, stripping listeners/chunk buffers, bounding concurrent :draining pairs (940 MiB e2-micro RAM / 1024 FD cap), and distinguishing read-FIN ('end' while backend still streams TLS response) from full close leaves stalled/scanner sockets pinning ~64 KiB+ TCPSocketWrap/ArrayBuffer slabs and closures for 5s (explaining overnight ~14 MiB/hr arrayBuffers drift), while premature :end-socket on client read-FIN aborts half-closed uploads/CONNECT streams.\n\n5. §2.1-§2.3 & §2.5.1-§2.5.2 Missing Paths, Allowlist Stripping & Browser Races (node_main.cljs, shell/light_node.clj, browser_main.cljs, shell/browser.cljc, light_node/core.cljc, config.cljc):\n- §2.1 misses run-mcp! (node_main.cljs:4539-4542, shell/light_node.clj:3988-3991), try-delegate-one-shot-to-daemon! (node_main.cljs:4186-4192), and run-daemon! 'ensure'/'start' (L4456-4463). Canonical :network-uri checks must strictly check (vals config/network-uris), NOT config/resolve-network-uri (config.cljc:69-73 echoes arbitrary strings like 'bitecho.org/dev'). In browser_main.cljs:242-265/623-643, :subnet-id is triplicated across [:subnet-id], [:light-state :subnet-id], and [:conn :subnet-id], and chat.js:1688/2162 passes subnetId: 'devnet.bitecho.org' on every initNode, clobbering persisted user subnet choices unless initial fallback vs explicit override is separated.\n- IndexedDB allowlist stripping: shell/browser.cljc:615-758 allowed-persistence-keys + sanitize-state-for-persistence (L802-819) filters recursively at all depths and will silently drop every new BIP-021 key (:subnet-id-reconciled, :session-tx-seq-rollback-*, :broadcast-sig-invalid, :broadcast-dac-*, :rolodex-seq, :subscribed-subnets) unless updated.\n- §2.2 & §2.3 gaps: build-session-ack-envelope (light_node/core.cljc:6766,6776) and exec-send (L3226) hardcode primary (:subnet-id state) instead of session/reply subnet-id, breaking replies across subscribed subnets; browser_main.cljs:665-669 poll-relay-envelopes! omits ?subnets=; and in §2.3, non-map non-nil wire-dac fails dac-valid? check without matching (map? wire-dac) (use (some? wire-dac)), while 'broadcast-rejected' lacks entry in actionable-event-types (L4358) and rate-limiting against log floods.\n- §2.5.1-§2.5.2 browser parity & auto-sync races: browser_cli/dispatch-browser-cli (browser_main.cljs:2687) must stay aligned with shell/browser.cljc:exec-browser-cli; tracking :relay-fallback-healthy? outside a single generation-tagged conn map violates Rule 4, and reporting transport_healthy: true with non-nil :last-error obscures degraded 1/6 mesh. Untracked init-node polling (L707) and keepalive-timers-atom (L1205) leak across stopNode (L2241) and apply-hardware-identity! (L199-212); auto-sync must store :generation, :active-pubkey, and AbortController inside node-atom, bound fetch timeouts < interval, supersede zombie pre-sleep fetches on hidden -> visible, and failover across multi-relay endpoints.\n\n6. §4 Open Questions — Explicit Answers:\n- Open Question 1 (§2.4 Auto-Advance vs Mandatory Re-Offer): Mandatory automatic X25519 p2p-offer re-key (auto-reoffer) + outbound send gate on rollback detection. Because crypto/sealed.cljc:917 uses deterministic (seq->nonce seq) under :tx-key, unrotated auto-advance cannot undo AEAD nonce reuse already committed before session-ack; if immediate catch-up sends are desired before re-key settles, sealed/seal-message must also add per-message CSPRNG salt/ratchet separation while still forcing immediate X25519 re-key, and handle-wire-sealed-msg must answer :stale-seq (lag >= 64) cleanly.\n- Open Question 2 (§2.5 Rolodex Pointer Namespace): Dedicated provisioned 'bitecho.org/rolodex' subnet hosted on ns1..ns3 with multi-subnet pointer routing in full_node_main.cljs/shell/http.clj, configured as :gossip-crdt (:gate/mode :permissionless or PoP) with :self-path-owner ACL 'rolodex/<pubkey>/*' (core/data.cljc:371-379). User primary subnets break recovery under arbitrary --subnet-id or wiped IndexedDB, while raw 'bitecho.org/infra' triggers :permissioned :allowlist rejection and mixes user churn into infra governance Merkle state.\n- Open Question 3 (§2.6 Mesh-First Updater Timeout Budget): Reject fixed 15,000 ms in favor of a two-tier BIP-017a chunked budget: a 2,500 ms fail-fast mesh probe/manifest timeout (preventing 15s stalls on relay-only or non-serving peers), paired with per-chunk 5,000 ms stall timeout over <= 192 KiB DataChannel / 1 MiB HTTP chunks up to min(45,000 ms, 5,000 ms + ceil(bytes / 256 KiB) * 1,000 ms) and per-chunk fallback to multi-relay HTTPS mirrors.",
