   "Advisory-only blind Round-1 review from :vector (Soak-Testing, VOPR, Staging Verification, Browser CDP E2E & Hive UI Lead), audited against /tmp/bip021-prep/bip-021-proposal.md (base b072e6a) and alpeware/hive HEAD 8318c2d (chat.js, chat.html, trace_viz.clj, trace_viz_test.clj, bip-018-pmem2-receipt.edn, bip-020-stage4-soak-and-cdp-receipt.edn). BIP-021's six pillars are directionally sound, but as written six concrete soak, Chrome CDP, Hive UI parity, and protocol-race blind spots allow production regressions to pass Stage 4 undetected:\n\n1. Gate 1 (P-MEM-1) & 2.6.1 (:443 Passthrough) miss ~14 MiB/hr overnight arrayBuffers drift & closure/handle leaks:\n   - In bip-018-pmem2-receipt.edn, offheap-gc-triggered runs every ~30s creating a ~20-28 MiB RSS sawtooth (177 -> 207 MiB pre-GC crests) and /statusz reported open-fds=nil (:open-fds-reported-in-digest? false). Gate 1's '>= 60 min' with '<= +5%' post-GC {rss, external, arrayBuffers} slope after 10m warmup fails to specify offheap-gc-edge-synchronized sampling or OLS linear regression, so endpoint aliasing can mask leaks, and +5% of ~190 MiB RSS permits +11.4 MiB/hr drift! Moreover, '0 leaked TCPSocketWrap handles' is unmeasurable until /statusz exposes active TCPSocketWrap, timer, /proc/self/fd, and passthrough active/draining pair counters.\n   - In 2.6.1, transition-passthrough-pair mentions 'clear drain timer' in prose for peer-closed? and :had-error?, but omits an explicit {:effect :clear-drain-timeout :pair-id ... :generation ...} effect, pinning closures/buffers up to 5000ms under churn. Gate 2 must also distinguish slow-draining multi-MiB TLS reads (where 5000ms idle vs total timeout must not cut off active reads) from backpressured peer-fin? half-closes (using paused/throttled TLS clients verifying 0 ECONNRESET/close_notify truncation) and stalled slowloris peers + HTTP CONNECT / DTLS ingress.\n\n2. 2.6.2 & Gate 5 (Mesh-First Auto-Update) break on real multi-MiB bundles & omit full_node_main.cljs:\n   - Bitecho WebRTC DataChannels enforce a=max-message-size:262144 (256 KiB), whereas real Stage 4 bundles are ~1.71 MiB (bitecho-light-node.cjs = 1,712,152 B; bitecho-full-node.cjs = 1,685,423 B) and JVM uberjars are >15 MiB. Unchunked single-envelope mesh artifact-get exceeds SCTP/wire limits on real bundles, guaranteeing 15s timeout stalls on every release while toy small-blob Gate 5 tests falsely pass. Also 2.6.2 omits full_node_main.cljs (:fetch-bundle-blob), and buffering multi-MiB bundles via exec-artifact-get hex strings risks doubling RAM on 940 MiB e2-micro hosts.\n\n3. 2.4 & Gate 4(d) (tx-seq Rollback) misses multi-message race & silently purges colliding frames:\n   - Checking (> peer-high-seq (long (:tx-seq session 0))) in handle-wire-session-ack fails completely when a rolled-back sender transmits >= 2 messages before the async session-ack returns (e.g., tx-seq rolls back 20->18, sender sends 19' and 20', leaving local-tx-seq=20 == peer-high-seq): (> 20 20) is false, zero mismatch diagnostic fires, BOTH 19' and 20' reused (tx-key, seq) AEAD nonces, and handle-wire-session-ack matches 19'/20' against the receiver's pre-rollback ack-seq/seen-seqs and purges them as delivered while the receiver dropped them as :replayed-seq!\n\n4. 2.5, Gate 6 & Companion alpeware/hive (chat.js HEAD 8318c2d, trace_viz.clj) Parity Blind Spots:\n   - shell/browser.cljc/allowed-persistence-keys is an allowlist: new fields (:reoffer-recommended?, :rolodex-seq, :rolodex-cid, :auto-sync-last-error, new diagnostics) will be stripped on IndexedDB save unless allowlisted (while keeping :connected?, :connection-error, :auto-sync-in-flight?, :rolodex-key unpersisted per Rule 4), and prune-ghost-sessions deletes restored 'open' sessions lacking :tx-key.\n   - 2.5.3 HKDF ('bitecho/rolodex-v1' + pubkey-hex) assumes an extractable raw secret in memory, which fails under chat.html's 'webcrypto-non-extractable' mode (extractable=false, sign/verify only) or locked hardware anchors without an explicit fail-closed :diagnose (:rolodex-key-unextractable / :hardware-unlock-required) or PRF/wrapped-KEK path.\n   - 2.5.2 :auto-sync-in-flight? lacks a generation-tagged timeout guard; a hung WebRTC chain-state-query or fetch wedges auto-sync permanently.\n   - In hive/resources/trace_viz/chat.js (HEAD 8318c2d): handleRecoverYubiKey (L1889) never invokes rolodex-restore; #btn-save-pn (L2093) and subscribeSubnet (L2111) never trigger debounced rolodex-put; custom subnets are split in localStorage ('hive_subscribed_subnets', L1458) bypassing node :subscribed-subnets on IndexedDB wipe; no UI surfaces session-seq-mismatch/reoffer_recommended, remote Rolodex :seq/encryption status, #btn-rolodex-restore, or ctl('status') fields (connected, transport_healthy, mesh_open_peers); and chat.html + trace_viz.clj (browser-bundle-sri) hardcode SHA-384 SRI for bitecho-browser.js which must be co-updated and tested via build-web-app! + COOP/COEP Chrome CDP against static /app/.\n   - Gate 6(d) fails to specify CDP WebAuthn.enable + WebAuthn.addVirtualAuthenticator (CTAP2 resident key/UV) + Storage.clearDataForOrigin + reload to actually exercise YubiKey-unlock-triggered rolodex-restore, and Gate 6(c) needs real CDP visibility transitions (Page.setWebLifecycleState or multi-tab Target.createTarget) with timer-jitter headroom (<= 75s).\n\n5. 2.1-2.3 & Gate 4(a-c) + Rule 6 Gaps:\n   - 2.1 CLI startup must detect explicit --subnet-id presence in argv vs parser default 'global' (Gate 4(a) must test both bare restart preserving persisted :subnet-id and explicit '--subnet-id global' override); Gate 4(b) must test negative rejections (unsubscribed subnet + outer/inner mismatch); 2.3/status must merge all new [:diagnostics ...] counters into ctl status & getStatus(); and Rule 6 requires co-committing --force (and --rolodex-subnet) into cli/known-command-flags, SKILL.md, docs/SPEC.md, populated-state smoke_light_node_live.sh, and hive/trace_viz.clj SRI.\n\nEXPLICIT ANSWERS TO SECTION 4 OPEN QUESTIONS:\n- Q1 (tx-seq Rollback Auto-Advance vs Mandatory Re-Offer): Neither naive auto-advance nor indefinite silent freeze is safe. Tag :replayed-seq session-ack replies with signed {:replay-rejected? true :rejected-seq msg-seq} so senders detect rollback even when local-tx-seq >= peer-high-seq and never falsely purge colliding outbox entries as delivered. On detection, mark the collided session :rekey-required (blocking new sends under the nonce-collided :tx-key so seq=21 never extends a compromised AES-GCM GHASH key) and automatically initiate p2p-offer key rotation (re-queueing un-delivered :rollback-collision plaintexts onto the rotated session); allow auto-advance + reoffer_recommended:true only as an explicit N-1 fallback when a peer lacks auto-rekey, surfaced loudly in chat.js and ctl status.\n- Q2 (Rolodex Pointer Namespace): Use a network-scoped canonical Rolodex subnet derived from :network-uri (e.g. 'bitecho.org/rolodex' on prod, overridable via --rolodex-subnet for devnet/staging) and auto-subscribe on startup—NOT the user's mutable primary chat :subnet-id (which forks or hides Rolodex across devices after 2.1 --subnet-id switches) and NOT an unscoped global literal that would cross-contaminate bitecho-gentoo-lab staging tests with live production pointers. Require 3/3 ns1..ns3 parity verification for rolodex/<pubkey-hex>/latest.enc in Stage 4.\n- Q3 (Mesh-First Updater Timeout Budget): Reject fixed 15,000 ms. Pair BIP-017a chunked mesh transfer (chunks <= 256 KiB to respect WebRTC SCTP a=max-message-size) with a two-tier watchdog: <= 3,000 ms initial metadata/TTFB ack (immediate HTTPS fallback on unconnected/artifact-missing), 5,000 ms per-chunk stall inactivity timeout (reset per SHA-256-verified chunk), and size-scaled total ceiling max(15,000 ms, min(120,000 ms, 5,000 + ceil(size_MiB) * 3,000)).",
